      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Came here to make this same suggestion.\n\nFirstly, the thumbnail of these worlds needs to be changed. Right now they say \"World CURRENTLY Unavailable\", which is inaccurate, since this only shows when the world has actually been deleted, as far as I'm aware. If it's set to Private, it says Private instead.\n\nSo, it should just more accurately say \"World Removed\" if nothing else. As currently it will make users feel like if they keep that favorite in their list, it might \"come back\", since it's only \"currently\" gone.\n\nIdeally at least the name & author of the world should be stored in our favorites data, (assuming that VRChat isn't keeping any database information about a deleted world ID that could be queried, I'd assume not for many reasons). That way, in the event a world is deleted, this thumbnail can at least say \"Blah blah World has been deleted. You should remove this favorite.\".\n\nThat way people can then search to see if a new version of that world has been made, and also click the creator's profile to see if maybe there's a world that's similar but under a new name now.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
